    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "executeQuery",
        "query": "-- 0048: each due step is claimed and its run moved on in one transaction, so\n-- a sweep that crashes half-way or overlaps the next one can't send a step\n-- twice. Runs with nothing to send (client replied or said STOP, lead closed,\n-- no steps left) are closed inside the function and don't come back here.\nselect * from claim_due_follow_up_runs(25);",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "828fa7a9-af45-41a3-8c54-c527ba566bf7",
      "name": "Query Due Runs",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.postgres",
      "typeVersion": 2.5,
      "position": [
        224,
        0
      ],
      "notesInFlow": true,
      "credentials": {
        "postgres": {
          "id": "TfAL8Z0epZ1Tqiib",
          "name": "Elliot Postgres (service role)"
        }
      },
      "notes": "Everything needed per due run in ONE query -- steps, contact info, autonomy_rules, AND the contact_replied check, all as a correlated subquery/join. Deliberately avoids chaining multiple Postgres nodes here: each one would either replace $json with just its RETURNING columns, or (worse) vanish the item entirely if it matched zero rows. One row per due run, capped at 25 per sweep so a backlog can't overload a single execution."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// One output item per due run (from Query Due Runs), paired with its input.\n// action: stop_replied | complete | send. For send, channel says how:\n//   whatsapp -- a WhatsApp step to a client who has written to the agency on\n//               WhatsApp (their opt-in), or an email step for a client with\n//               no email address but a WhatsApp chat;\n//   email    -- an email step, or a WhatsApp step for a client who has never\n//               written on WhatsApp (WhatsApp would refuse it);\n//   none     -- no way to reach the client: the step is skipped.\n// WhatsApp after 24 hours goes inside the approved template; workflow 27\n// decides that when it sends (an approval can take longer than 24 hours).\nconst out = [];\n$input.all().forEach((item, i) => {\n  const r = item.json;\n  const steps = Array.isArray(r.steps) ? r.steps : [];\n  if (r.contact_replied) {\n    out.push({ json: { action: 'stop_replied', run_id: r.run_id }, pairedItem: i });\n    return;\n  }\n  const step = steps[r.current_step_index];\n  if (!step) {\n    out.push({ json: { action: 'complete', run_id: r.run_id }, pairedItem: i });\n    return;\n  }\n  const isFinal = r.current_step_index === steps.length - 1;\n  const nextStep = isFinal ? null : steps[r.current_step_index + 1];\n\n  const contactName = r.contact_name || 'there';\n  const fill = (t) => String(t || '').replace(/\\{\\{\\s*contact_name\\s*\\}\\}/g, contactName);\n  const body = fill(step.body);\n\n  const email = String(r.contact_email || '').trim();\n  const waId = String(r.contact_phone || '').replace(/\\D/g, '');\n  const onWhatsApp = !!(r.wa_conversation_id && r.wa_last_inbound_at && waId.length >= 8 && r.whatsapp_phone_number_id);\n  const wanted = step.channel === 'whatsapp' ? 'whatsapp' : 'email';\n  const channel = wanted === 'whatsapp'\n    ? (onWhatsApp ? 'whatsapp' : email ? 'email' : 'none')\n    : (email ? 'email' : onWhatsApp ? 'whatsapp' : 'none');\n  // A WhatsApp step sent by email needs a subject: the message's first line.\n  const firstLine = body.trim().split('\\n')[0].replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim();\n  const subject = fill(step.subject) || (firstLine.length > 70 ? firstLine.slice(0, 67).trimEnd() + '…' : firstLine) || 'Following up';\n\n  const mode = r.autonomy_rules?.send_follow_up?.mode === 'autonomous' ? 'autonomous' : 'approval_required';\n  out.push({\n    json: {\n      action: 'send',\n      channel,\n      run_id: r.run_id,\n      tenant_id: r.tenant_id,\n      contact_id: r.contact_id,\n      contact_email: email || null,\n      from_email: r.connected_gmail_address || null,\n      subject,\n      body,\n      to_wa_id: onWhatsApp ? waId : null,\n      phone_number_id: r.whatsapp_phone_number_id || null,\n      wa_conversation_id: r.wa_conversation_id || null,\n      wa_last_inbound_at: r.wa_last_inbound_at || null,\n      mode,\n      draft_status: mode === 'autonomous' ? 'auto_sent' : 'pending',\n      is_final: isFinal,\n      next_step_day_offset: nextStep ? (nextStep.day_offset ?? 0) : null,\n    },\n    pairedItem: i,\n  });\n});\nreturn out;"
      },
